<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=gas-lighting">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Energy and power</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gas lighting</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1792">1792</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gas lighting is the production of artificial light by burning a fuel gas, principally <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a> gas in the period when it was widespread. William Murdoch first lit his own house in Redruth, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cornwall">Cornwall</a>, in 1792, lit the main building of the Soho Foundry in 1798 and the outside in a public display in 1802. Friedrich Winzer patented coal-gas lighting in 1804, and gas street lighting reached Salford in 1806 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> in 1820. It spread through European and North American cities, and electric lighting displaced it from the late 19th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gas-lighting.jpg" alt="Gas lighting" width="330" height="440" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Aw58 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wrocław,_kościół_pw._śś._Piotra_i_Pawła_DSCF0144.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Gas lighting</b> spread rapidly through British cities over the next decades.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/january-28">28 January in history</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>1792</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Redruth, Cornwall, England</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd>William Murdoch</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Also arose independently</span>Paris, France (1801)</p><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Chinese records dating back 1,700 years indicate natural gas carried by bamboo pipes for lighting and heating in homes.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/coal">Coal<span>25,000–23,000 BCE</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=gas-lighting">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
